 "system": {
  "description": "<ul><li><strong>Effect:</strong> As an action, curse one creature within <strong>30ft</strong> — <strong>Will save</strong> or have <strong>Disadvantage</strong> on one of: attack rolls, saving throws, or ability checks (your choice when you cast it) for the encounter.</li><li>While hexed, it also takes <strong>1d6</strong> necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns (<strong>2d6</strong> at 5th, <strong>3d6</strong> at 9th, <strong>4d6</strong> at 13th, <strong>5d6</strong> at 17th), and repeats the <strong>Will save</strong> at the end of each of its turns, ending the Hex on a success.</li><li>The <strong>Disadvantage</strong> never applies to saves against the Hex itself.</li><li>You can have only one Hex active; a new Hex ends the old one.</li><li>You can Hex for free a number of times per day equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum 1); each further Hex costs a 1st-level slot.</li><li>Patron Boon — Buff: gain the 1st-tier Buff granted by your chosen Patron</li></ul>",
